                    brief_y10:               `Year 10. Mid-life of production. A visiting Skarvheim Kapitalforvaltning advisor reminds the Council that the Norwegian framework rests on six institutional pillars, none free.`,
                    brief_y11:               `Year 11. Peak prices return. A new populist government takes office and threatens the savings rule. Constitutional protection of the fund, if it exists, is now load-bearing.`,
                    brief_y12:               `Year 12. Production begins to decline. Long-horizon institutional investments — schools, ports, technical training — are now non-deferrable. So is post-extraction planning.`,
                    brief_y13:               `Year 13. Stranded-asset risk rises with global climate policy. Discounted reserves are now smaller than the geological audit suggested, and traders expect the sharpest one-year fall in the gas price since production began. Future royalties face a haircut.`,
                    brief_y14:               `Year 14. Late decline. The post-extraction economic structure must already be visible in the data. If tradables collapsed, recovery is a generation away.`,
